{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c383","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a14b74-03fb-7d03-878f-dfaf07bafb31"},"sequence":28,"recorded_at":1780531400000051,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a14b74-0c73-7f61-b488-8792254708ab","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"01a14b74-0c73-7f61-b488-8792254708ab","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"01a14b74-0c73-7f61-b488-8792254708ab"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a14b74-4a3b-76d3-8ef1-f84d1fbf56c6"},"task_id":"01a14b74-4a3b-76d3-8ef1-f84d1fbf56c6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a14b74-4a3b-76d3-8ef1-f84d1fbf56c6","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/.ai-team/runs/dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017/code-review-package.md`.\n1|# Code Review Package — dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017\n2|\n3|## 1. Metadata & Artifact Hashes\n4|- **Task ID**: `dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017`\n5|- **Jira Issue**: [EYE-33873](https://tasks.sberdevices.ru/browse/EYE-33873)\n6|- **Criticality**: `S2` (`parent_skill=analyst-teamlead`, downstream panel)\n7|- **Architecture Spec**: `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/.ai-team/runs/dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017/architecture/arch-spec.md`\n8|- **Architecture Packet**: `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/.ai-team/runs/dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017/architecture/architecture-packet.json` (`sha256=86de86783a9eaba1d866955443f59cc31da128d715585456898b9590100ed206`)\n9|- **ARCH_PANEL Proof (Round r2)**: `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/.ai-team/runs/dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017/panel/arch/r2/panel-proof.json` (`sha256=564c5afab8e1890222f84bba898f881826f98d4108758eddf2e13a11820d3e69`)\n10|- **Coder Plan**: `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/.ai-team/runs/dsh-bridge-resilience-20261017/plans/coder-01.json` (`sha256=c33259b6f5fdad2d4d99ba138bbeb623e2034a3391895eb09724a45a294e4273`)\n11|- **ADR Document**: `/Users/aazhiry1/work/src/cli-agent-bridge/docs/adr/0005-resilient-hub-lifecycle-and-detached-turns.md`\n12|- **Baseline Git Commit**: `d00d698` (`docs(readme): explain official vendor CLIs vs OAuth proxies (CLIProxyAPI)`)\n13|\n14|## 2. Traceability Matrix: Requirements & Arch Decisions (RW-001..RW-010)\n15|| Requirement / Finding | Architecture Decision & Implementation | Implementation Path | Tests |\n16||---|---|---|---|\n17|| **User Directive 1 & RW-001/002**: Detached turn execution on socket drop (`client_gone`) without killing subagent | `ManagedTurn`, `TurnSessionManager`, `TurnBuffer` ring buffer 10MB, `POST/DELETE /v1/turns/<id>/cancel`, `DETACHED_ORPHAN_TTL_S = 300.0` | `core/turn_session_manager.py`, `server.py` | `tests/test_detached_turn_execution.py`, `tests/test_turn_cancel_and_gap.py` |\n18|| **User Directive 2 & RW-006**: Adaptive idle watchdog (300s) + cputime child monitoring on Darwin + safety cap (3600s) | `AdaptiveTimeoutController`, `ProcessWatchdog` parsing `cputime` across child pgid, fail-closed on `ps` failure | `core/watchdog.py` | `tests/test_adaptive_idle_watchdog.py` |\n19|| **User Directive 3**: Resilience in common hub core layer (`core/`), not per-adapter | Extracted `core/turn_session_manager.py`, `core/watchdog.py`, `core/lifecycle.py`, `core/backend_adapter.py` | `core/` | All test suites |\n20|| **RW-003**: Deterministic turn key | `turn_key = sha256(turn_id:rid:session_id)` prevents collision or reuse across rids | `core/turn_session_manager.py` | `tests/test_detached_turn_execution.py` |\n21|| **RW-004**: Gap Replay detection | Buffer evictions return HTTP 410 `GAP_DETECTED` on reattach with stale `Last-Event-ID` | `core/turn_session_manager.py`, `server.py` | `tests/test_turn_cancel_and_gap.py` |\n22|| **RW-005**: Graceful shutdown & drain | `HubLifecycleManager`, non-blocking signal handling via `threading.Event`, drain timeout 110s, 503 `Retry-After: 5` | `core/lifecycle.py`, `server.py` | `tests/test_graceful_shutdown_drain.py` |\n23|| **RW-007**: Safe turn disk serialization | Atomic write to `~/.dsh/turns/<id>.json` with schema version 1.0, 0600 file mode, directory 0700 | `core/turn_session_manager.py` | `tests/test_detached_turn_execution.py` |\n24|| **RW-008**: Security input validation | Strict regex `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$` on all `turn_id` path and query params | `server.py`, `bridges/muse-bridge/server.py` | `tests/test_turn_cancel_and_gap.py` |\n25|| **RW-009**: Feature flags | `DSH_BRIDGE_DETACHED_ENABLED`, `DSH_BRIDGE_WATCHDOG_ENABLED`, `DSH_BRIDGE_DRAIN_ENABLED` defaults | `server.py` | Unit tests |\n26|| **RW-010**: DSH profile syntax fix | Remove invalid `{{cwd}}` from persona-suffix in `~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml` | `~/.dsh/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml` | `tests/test_dsh_profile_config.py` |\n27|\n28|## 3. Test Suites & Verification Evidence\n29|- **New Unit Tests** (15 tests, 0.56s execution):\n30|  - `tests/test_detached_turn_execution.py` (4 tests: detached background finish, reattach streaming, disk persistence, memory buffer)\n31|  - `tests/test_adaptive_idle_watchdog.py` (4 tests: idle reset on tokens, safety cap enforcement, Darwin ps parsing, fail-closed)\n32|  - `tests/test_graceful_shutdown_drain.py` (3 tests: SIGTERM signal event, active turn drain, 503 Retry-After rejection)\n33|  - `tests/test_turn_cancel_and_gap.py` (3 tests: explicit cancel endpoint, gap 410 detection, orphan TTL reaper)\n34|  - `tests/test_dsh_profile_config.py` (1 test: cordis patch yml validation)\n35|- **Regression Tests**: 208 existing unit and integration tests passing in 122.8s.\n36|- **Code Linter**: `ruff check` passed without any warnings or errors.\n37|\n38|## 4. Full Git Diff (`git diff HEAD`)\n39|```diff\n40|diff --git a/README.md b/README.md\n41|index 32c8f24..f2b7c2b 100644\n42|--- a/README.md\n43|+++ b/README.md\n44|@@ -74,13 +74,13 @@ or script that speaks the OpenAI protocol.\n45| \n46| ## Why official vendor CLIs instead of OAuth proxies (CLIProxyAPI)\n47| \n48|-When direct pay-as-you-go API keys are not used, this hub (`droid exec`, `muse serve`) and its sibling bridges (`claude -p`, `cursor-agent -p`, `agy -p`, `opencode`) spawn the official vendor CLI as a local child process instead of extracting OAuth tokens and calling cloud APIs over raw HTTP like [CLIProxyAPI](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI) (`cliproxy`).\n49|+This hub contains no OAuth handling. It starts the official vendor CLI as a local child process (`droid exec` for the `droid` backend, `muse exec` for the `muse` backend) and returns that CLI's answer through the OpenAI-compatible API. The sibling bridges (`claude -p`, `cursor-agent -p`, `agy -p`, `opencode`) follow the same pattern but live outside this repository. [CLIProxyAPI](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI) (`cliproxy`) takes the other route: it stores OAuth logins for many accounts and sends HTTP requests to provider APIs itself.\n50| \n51| Replaying subscription tokens through an OAuth proxy carries three risks:\n52| \n53|-- **Account bans and subscription revocations.** Providers can ban accounts or revoke subscriptions when OAuth tokens issued to an official vendor CLI are replayed from an external OAuth proxy. Spawning the official vendor CLI avoids HTTP client impersonation, though it does not exempt automated usage from each provider's terms of service or guarantee against policy enforcement.\n54|-- **Anthropic and other official vendor CLIs cannot be faithfully reproduced over HTTP.** As shown in CLIProxyAPI's [utls_transport.go](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/blob/main/internal/auth/claude/utls_transport.go) and [claude_executor_cloaking.go](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/blob/main/internal/runtime/executor/claude_executor_cloaking.go), mimicking Claude Code (`claude`) over raw HTTP requires custom TLS `ClientHello` fingerprints (`utls`), injected `metadata.user_id` values, salted `x-anthropic-billing-header` hashes (`SHA256(salt + messageText[4,7,20] + version)`), and prompt cloaking of sensitive words.\n55|-- **Server-side detection rules change without notice.** Because client checks are enforced on the provider's servers, rotating the fingerprint salt, checking a new header or telemetry field, or flagging cloaked prompts breaks external OAuth proxies or triggers bans without a client release. The trade-off of the local bridge model is operational: each host must install, authenticate, and update the official vendor CLI binaries.\n56|+- **Account bans and subscription revocations.** Providers can ban accounts or revoke subscriptions when OAuth tokens are replayed from an external proxy. Running the official CLI avoids client impersonation, but it does not make automated use allowed under each provider's terms of service, and it does not guarantee against enforcement.\n57|+- **Client imitation is fragile.** To pass as Claude Code over raw HTTP, CLIProxyAPI copies the client's TLS fingerprint for OAuth requests ([utls_transport.go](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/blob/main/internal/auth/claude/utls_transport.go)), injects a fake `metadata.user_id`, computes a 3-character build fingerprint for `x-anthropic-billing-header` from a fixed salt, three sampled prompt characters, and the client version, and obfuscates configured sensitive words in prompts ([claude_executor_cloaking.go](https://github.com/router-for-me/CLIProxyAPI/blob/main/internal/runtime/executor/claude_executor_cloaking.go)). Its code targets specific Claude Code versions, and this was checked for Claude Code only.\n58|+- **Server-side detection rules can change at any time.** Client checks run on the provider's servers. A new salt, header, telemetry field, or prompt check can break an external OAuth proxy or get its accounts flagged, with no new client release. The cost of the local-CLI model is operational: each host must install, sign in to, and update the vendor CLI binaries.\n59| \n60| ## Supported backends and connected agent CLIs\n61| \n62|@@ -111,12 +111,13 @@ documented below and in the [port map](#ecosystem-port-and-architecture-map).\n63| \n64| ### `muse` — Meta Muse CLI (in-tree hub and dedicated bridge)\n65| \n66|-- Transport: `muse serve` (MSP — Muse Server Protocol, JSON-RPC over\n67|+- Transport: headless `muse exec` per turn through the launcher wrapper\n68|+  (`~/.config/muse-launch/muse-cli.sh`). The dedicated `muse-bridge` (port\n69|+  `9886`) uses `muse serve` (MSP — Muse Server Protocol, JSON-RPC over\n70|   stdin/stdout) with `approvalMode: \"allowAll\"` on `session/start`\n71|-  ([ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-muse-serve-approval-allowall.md)), so interactive\n72|-  multi-step sessions run without a turn reset; headless one-shot `muse exec`\n73|-  through a launcher wrapper remains available. Wonder context is pruned\n74|-  (400k/320k/200k) and net-timeouts are retried.\n75|+  ([ADR 0003](docs/adr/0003-muse-serve-approval-allowall.md)), so its\n76|+  interactive multi-step sessions run without a turn reset. Wonder context is\n77|+  pruned (400k/320k/200k) and net-timeouts are retried.\n78| - Tool access: Full Access — models can read and write files and run shell\n79|   commands (`--disable-write` / `--disable-shell` are no longer passed).\n80| - Streaming: live `reasoning_content` with the model's thoughts (`summary.*`\n81|@@ -182,7 +183,7 @@ arbitrary code, so a new CLI always lands as explicit, reviewable code plus\n82| | Port | Service / bridge | Backend CLI / engine | Models served | Key characteristics |\n83| |---|---|---|---|---|\n84| | `:9881` | `claude-p-bridge` | `claude -p` | `claude-opus-5-5`, `claude-haiku-5-5` | Dedicated CLI bridge, tool-calling emulation |\n85|-| `:9882` | `cli-agent-bridge` (hub, this repo) | `droid exec` + `muse serve` | `claude-sonnet-5-5`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, `grok-4.7`, `gpt-6.1-sol`, `muse-wonder-1.0` | Multi-binary hub, resident sessions, catalog schema 3 |\n86|+| `:9882` | `cli-agent-bridge` (hub, this repo) | `droid exec` + `muse exec` | `claude-sonnet-5-5`, `gemini-3.8-flash`, `grok-4.7`, `gpt-6.1-sol`, `muse-wonder-1.0` (Muse enabled only) | Multi-binary hub, resident sessions, catalog schema 3 |\n87| | `:9884` | `claude-p-sonnet-bridge` | `claude -p` | `claude-sonnet-5-5` | Dedicated Sonnet 5.5 bridge |\n88| | `:9885` | `grok46-bridge` / `agy-bridge` | `cursor-agent -p` / `agy -p` | `cursor-grok-4.6-high`, `gemini-4-argon` | 500k context, stdin streaming, progressive thinking |\n89| | `:9886` | `muse-bridge` | `muse serve` + `muse exec` | `muse-wonder-1.0`, `muse-spark-1.3` | MSP JSON-RPC, `allowAll` approval, live reasoning |\n90|diff --git a/adapters/droid_adapter.py b/adapters/droid_adapter.py\n91|index b34b485..1f36fbc 100644\n92|--- a/adapters/droid_adapter.py\n93|+++ b/adapters/droid_adapter.py\n94|@@ -80,7 +80,20 @@ class DroidAdapter(BackendAdapter):\n95|         legacy[\"rpc\"][\"items\"] = [asdict(item) for item in ctx.rpc.items]\n96|         legacy[\"images\"] = [asdict(image) for image in ctx.images]\n97|         handler = cast(Any, ctx.handler)\n98|-        raw = handler._run_once(legacy, ctx.keepalive, sse_writer)\n99|+        if callable(ctx.on_activity):\n100|+            ctx.on_activity(\"start\")\n101|+        wrapped_writer: Optional[StreamSink] = None\n102|+        if sse_writer is not None:\n103|+\n104|+            def _wrapped_writer(kind: str, text: str) -> bool:\n105|+                if callable(ctx.on_activity):\n106|+                    ctx.on_activity(kind)\n107|+                return sse_writer(kind, text)\n108|+\n109|+            wrapped_writer = _wrapped_writer\n110|+        raw = handler._run_once(legacy, ctx.keepalive, wrapped_writer)\n111|+        if callable(ctx.on_activity):\n112|+            ctx.on_activity(\"done\")\n113|         usage = raw.get(\"usage\") or {}\n114| \n115|         def tool_call(call: dict) -> ToolCall:\n116|diff --git a/adapters/muse_adapter.py b/adapters/muse_adapter.py\n117|index 3bfd703..ec6da21 100644\n118|--- a/adapters/muse_adapte